{
  "schema_version": "1.1",
  "scenario_id": "date_to_timestamp",
  "title": "Date column becomes a timestamp at midnight",
  "category": "temporal",
  "description": "A date32 column becomes a naive timestamp[us] column of the same name. Each value becomes 00:00:00 of the same day. Values include the day before the epoch, the epoch, a leap day, 0001-01-01 and 9999-12-31, and a null.",
  "notes": [
    "Iceberg v3 lists date to timestamp as a type promotion, and Delta type widening allows date to timestampNTZ.",
    "At the Parquet level the logical type changes from DATE (INT32 days) to a Timestamp in MICROS (INT64) with isAdjustedToUTC false.",
    "timestamp[ns] holds 1677-09-21 to 2262-04-11. Promoting 0001-01-01 or 9999-12-31 to nanoseconds has no value for those rows."
  ],
  "tags": [
    "change-type",
